Phase OS-12: Kernel Cryptographic Subsystem - 3 new kernel ASM modules:

1. kernel/crypto_aes.asm (AES Block Cipher)
   - AArch64 ASM implementation of AES (FIPS 197)
   - AES-128/192/256 key sizes (10/12/14 rounds)
   - Key expansion: round key generation with Rcon, RotWord, SubWord
   - Core operations: SubBytes (S-box lookup), ShiftRows, MixColumns, AddRoundKey
   - Modes of operation: ECB, CBC (with IV), CTR (counter mode), GCM (authenticated)
   - AES-NI / ARM CE acceleration: use AESE/AESMC instructions if available
   - Padding: PKCS#7 for block cipher modes
   - Export symbols: crypto_aes_init, crypto_aes_set_key, crypto_aes_encrypt, crypto_aes_decrypt, crypto_aes_cbc_encrypt, crypto_aes_gcm_encrypt
   - Integration: called by net_tls.asm for record encryption, by filesystem for at-rest encryption

2. kernel/crypto_sha.asm (SHA-2 Hash Functions)
   - AArch64 ASM implementation of SHA-2 family (FIPS 180-4)
   - SHA-224: 224-bit digest, 64 rounds
   - SHA-256: 256-bit digest, 64 rounds (most common)
   - SHA-384: 384-bit digest, 80 rounds
   - SHA-512: 512-bit digest, 80 rounds
   - HMAC: keyed-hash message authentication (RFC 2104)
   - ARM SHA-2 acceleration: use SHA256H/SHA256H2/SHA256SU0/SHA256SU1 instructions
   - Streaming: init/update/final API for incremental hashing
   - Export symbols: crypto_sha_init, crypto_sha256_update, crypto_sha256_final, crypto_sha512_update, crypto_hmac_sha256
   - Integration: called by net_tls.asm for PRF/handshake hashes, by secure_boot.asm for image verification

3. kernel/crypto_rng.asm (Cryptographic Random Number Generation)
   - AArch64 ASM implementation of secure random number generation
   - Entropy source: ARM RNDR/RNDRRS instructions (TRNG hardware), cycle counter fallback
   - CSPRNG: CTR-DRBG (NIST SP 800-90A) with AES-256 core
   - Entropy pool: 256-byte pool, continuous health testing
   - Seeding: automatic reseed every 2^20 requests, manual reseed support
   - Output: random bytes, random integers (uniform), random UUIDs (v4)
   - Prediction resistance: reseed before each generate if flag set
   - Export symbols: crypto_rng_init, crypto_rng_seed, crypto_rng_bytes, crypto_rng_int, crypto_rng_uuid
   - Integration: called by net_tls.asm for nonces, by crypto_aes.asm for IV generation

All modules follow existing kernel conventions (.arch armv8-a, .global exports, stp/ldp frame setup).
